      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_10e8ca8c1b7656d665b62d0d7a1b1f94e5e1b75b76d61d98d336b466e4b89e3c",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "For the dilation setting, symplectic area and leading smooth counts survive changes of phase-space presentation, but regulator-dependent terms and quantum interpretation do not. The Connes-Consani map preserves area while retaining a later Maslov-sign distinction; the Berry-Keating and Connes cutoffs give opposite finite-count readings; and the finite inverse model reproduces the leading Connes-type term but requires incompatible cutoff identifications to match the linear term. Coarse count agreement therefore does not establish quantum or spectral equivalence.",
