    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_644aebf5dd57af6ab1401ec232e94ac7ab797da7475face6b9850e2f4d3f511d",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Arithmetic spectral statistics must be indexed by both operator and orbit mechanism. Sarnak's arithmetic quotients have infinitely many nonlocal Hecke correspondences commuting with the Laplacian and redirect the random-matrix comparison from exceptional Laplace levels to Hecke spectra. Bogomolny's non-arithmetic triangles show that exponential orbit-length multiplicity alone is not the converse diagnostic: under the assumed multiplicity law, an exponent below one half leaves the diagonal form factor vanishing within its shrinking range of validity despite reported GOE-like spacings.",
