      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_87cdd30f2a48d9f32aa2fdea5ced2f88c8125e2a345815976d2a8182213d0aa6",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The residue calculation constructs a scalar representation of zeta in a stated strip by turning coefficient powers into a summable kernel. The Fourier construction performs a different lift: for a chosen scalar F it defines F of the flat d'Alembertian modewise by multiplication with F(k squared). The concrete bridge is a construction ladder from scalar analytic data to a Fourier multiplier; the second step additionally depends on geometry, a field class, convergence, and an operator domain, so a scalar kernel is not yet a self-adjoint spectral realization.",
