    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_c8ac40d35dbea008a3d2979e09c3e906985ba9c8efc041aca9b5be2750f76207",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The proposed unification is not supported. Centrality and Hamiltonian commutation make the black-hole phase-space identification group-compatible and dynamically covariant, while that source separately leaves absorption versus emission, microstate adequacy, and a spectrum unbounded below unresolved. A different paper's missing domain, adjoint, completeness, and self-adjointness for its difference Hamiltonian cannot be imported as the mechanism that resolves those physical questions.",
